         <p>Front cover</p>
         <head>DAME WONDER’S<lb/>PICTURE<lb/>ALPHABET.</head>
         <pb/>
         <div type="div1">
            <head>Dame Wonder's Picture Alphabet / Amusing Alphabet, Dame Wonder's Series.</head>
            <p rend="justify">Title page</p>
            <lg>
               <l>A stands for an Archer,</l>
               <l>B for his Bow;</l>
               <l>C the Crow that he shot at;—and</l>
               <l>D for his Dog.</l>
            </lg>
            <lg>
               <l>E stands for an Ensign,</l>
               <l>F for a Flag, and a Fort:</l>
               <l>G stands for a Goat;—and</l>
               <l>H for a Horse.</l>
            </lg>
            <lg>
               <l>I stands for an Italian,</l>
               <l>J for a Jug, and for Jane:</l>
               <l>K stands for a Kite:—and</l>
               <l>L for a Lobster.</l>
            </lg>
            <lg>
               <l>M stands for Mary,</l>
               <l>N for the Numbers she wrote;</l>
               <l>O stands for an Owl:—and</l>
               <l>P for a pretty Parrot.</l>
            </lg>
            <lg>
               <l>Q stands for a Queen,</l>
               <l>R for the Rose in her hand:</l>
               <l>S for the Sword of State,</l>
               <l>T the Throne, and the Table.</l>
            </lg>
            <lg>
               <l>U stands for Uncle, V for Violin,</l>
               <l>W for Windmill, and X for number ten</l>
               <l>Y stands for a Yacht, (or Yot,)—and</l>
               <l>Z for a Zebra.</l>
            </lg>
